face, I duck

33:01.680 --> 33:02.060
instantly.

33:02.220 --> 33:02.660
I flinch.

33:02.900 --> 33:03.560
I certainly

33:03.560 --> 33:04.060
didn't spend

33:04.060 --> 33:04.640
hours in my

33:04.640 --> 33:05.860
childhood deliberately

33:05.860 --> 33:06.620
and explicitly

33:06.620 --> 33:07.480
coordinating the

33:07.480 --> 33:08.220
mechanics of my

33:08.220 --> 33:09.140
flinching mechanism.

33:09.620 --> 33:10.560
Or if I taste

33:10.560 --> 33:11.460
something incredibly

33:11.460 --> 33:12.220
bitter, I instantly

33:12.220 --> 33:12.740
recoil.

33:13.160 --> 33:13.940
I didn't practice

33:13.940 --> 33:14.280
that.

33:14.880 --> 33:15.940
That is a

33:15.940 --> 33:17.000
critical objection,

33:17.340 --> 33:18.180
and it's one that

33:18.180 --> 33:19.460
any robust theory of

33:19.460 --> 33:20.140
cognition has to

33:20.140 --> 33:20.460
address.

33:21.360 --> 33:22.260
Flyxion addresses

33:22.260 --> 33:22.960
it head-on in

33:22.960 --> 33:23.860
chapter 7 by

33:23.860 --> 33:24.680
setting very

33:24.680 --> 33:25.540
clear boundaries.

33:26.360 --> 33:27.220
Aspect relegation

33:27.220 --> 33:28.560
theory is not an

33:28.560 --> 33:29.360
absolutist theory.

33:29.800 --> 33:30.860
It does not claim

33:30.860 --> 33:31.680
that all

33:31.680 --> 33:33.140
automaticity is the

33:33.140 --> 33:33.960
result of compressed

33:33.960 --> 33:34.680
deliberation.

33:34.680 --> 33:35.700
Okay, so it

33:35.700 --> 33:36.380
admits there are

33:36.380 --> 33:36.840
exceptions.

33:37.920 --> 33:38.740
It categorizes

33:38.740 --> 33:39.820
automaticity into

33:39.820 --> 33:40.800
different historical

33:40.800 --> 33:41.160
routes.

33:41.720 --> 33:42.400
The first boundary,

33:42.700 --> 33:43.420
the exception you

33:43.420 --> 33:44.640
just described, is

33:44.640 --> 33:46.160
hardwired evolutionary

33:46.160 --> 33:47.000
reflexes.

33:47.160 --> 33:47.640
Like flinching.

33:47.940 --> 33:49.100
Yes, flinching from

33:49.100 --> 33:50.840
a projectile, low-level

33:50.840 --> 33:52.160
perceptual binding like

33:52.160 --> 33:53.040
depth perception,

33:53.040 --> 33:54.680
basic affective

33:54.680 --> 33:55.420
valences like

33:55.420 --> 33:56.360
recoiling from a

33:56.360 --> 33:56.880
bitter taste.

33:57.260 --> 33:58.120
These are hardwired.

33:58.460 --> 33:59.240
They are fixed by

33:59.240 --> 34:00.280
evolution and

34:00.280 --> 34:01.380
biological development.

34:01.780 --> 34:02.480
They operate

34:02.480 --> 34:03.580
automatically without

34:03.580 --> 34:04.440
ever having been

34:04.440 --> 34:05.220
acquired through the

34:05.220 --> 34:06.260
agent's own practice.

34:06.600 --> 34:07.380
And Flyxion is okay

34:07.380 --> 34:07.760
with that?

34:08.020 --> 34:08.440
Absolutely.

34:08.960 --> 34:09.880
Flyxion acknowledges

34:09.880 --> 34:10.920
this as a genuine,

34:11.480 --> 34:12.480
entirely separate

34:12.480 --> 34:12.940
source of

34:12.940 --> 34:13.820
automaticity without

34:13.820 --> 34:14.860
any embarrassment to

34:14.860 --> 34:15.520
the core theory.

34:15.980 --> 34:16.800
Okay, so the theory

34:16.800 --> 34:17.660
is mostly applying to

34:17.660 --> 34:18.900
learned competencies,

34:19.280 --> 34:20.200
the higher-level stuff

34:20.200 --> 34:21.300
we actually care about in

34:21.300 --> 34:22.100
debates over human

34:22.100 --> 34:22.780
rationality.

34:23.280 --> 34:23.880
Root selection,

34:24.220 --> 34:24.900
social inference,

34:25.140 --> 34:26.020
strategic choice,

34:26.280 --> 34:27.040
language processing.

34:27.400 --> 34:27.880
Exactly.

34:28.220 --> 34:29.460
The competencies that

34:29.460 --> 34:30.720
the System 1 and

34:30.720 --> 34:31.600
System 2 framework

34:31.600 --> 34:32.500
are actually used to

34:32.500 --> 34:32.780
debate.

34:33.440 --> 34:34.080
No one is writing

34:34.080 --> 34:35.140
behavioral economics

34:35.140 --> 34:36.000
papers about the

34:36.000 --> 34:37.040
rationality of the

34:37.040 --> 34:37.740
flinch reflex.

34:38.220 --> 34:38.960
Fair point, yeah.

34:39.500 --> 34:40.440
But even within those

34:40.440 --> 34:41.800
learned, higher-level

34:41.800 --> 34:42.480
competencies,

34:43.020 --> 34:43.920
Flyxion notes there

34:43.920 --> 34:44.940
are other routes to

34:44.940 --> 34:45.880
automaticity besides

34:45.880 --> 34:47.000
your own deliberate

34:47.000 --> 34:47.500
practice.

34:48.000 --> 34:48.540
For instance,

34:48.780 --> 34:49.140
conditioning.

34:49.140 --> 34:50.180
Conditioning.

34:50.860 --> 34:52.120
Like Pavlov's dog

34:52.120 --> 34:53.120
salivating at a bell?

34:54.080 --> 34:55.320
Or more relevant to

34:55.320 --> 34:56.100
our modern lives,

34:56.480 --> 34:56.920
advertising.

34:57.260 --> 34:57.400
Right.

34:57.740 --> 34:59.000
Consider a masterfully

34:59.000 --> 35:00.280
engineered advertising

35:00.280 --> 35:00.720
campaign.

35:01.160 --> 35:02.060
An external actor,

35:02.180 --> 35:02.820
the advertiser,

35:03.440 --> 35:04.220
engineers your

35:04.220 --> 35:05.020
exposure history.

35:05.620 --> 35:06.700
They repeatedly pair

35:06.700 --> 35:07.640
their brand of soda

35:07.640 --> 35:08.600
with images of

35:08.600 --> 35:09.180
happiness,

35:09.440 --> 35:10.160
attractive people,

35:10.420 --> 35:11.220
and catchy music.

35:11.440 --> 35:12.300
They force it on you.

35:12.380 --> 35:13.280
Yeah, they force a

35:13.280 --> 35:14.120
stabilization of

35:14.120 --> 35:15.160
associations in your

35:15.160 --> 35:16.260
mind that you didn't

35:16.260 --> 35:17.520
deliberately choose to

35:17.520 --> 35:18.120
solve a problem.

35:18.120 --> 35:19.420
Eventually, you see

35:19.420 --> 35:20.340
the logo and you

35:20.340 --> 35:21.440
automatically feel a

35:21.440 --> 35:22.320
positive association.

35:23.020 --> 35:23.280
Wow.

35:23.460 --> 35:25.020
The automaticity belongs

35:25.020 --> 35:25.500
to you.

35:25.740 --> 35:26.780
It resides in your

35:26.780 --> 35:27.120
brain.

35:27.600 --> 35:28.360
But the stabilization

35:28.360 --> 35:29.940
process was hijacked

35:29.940 --> 35:30.580
and built by an

35:30.580 --> 35:31.420
external actor.

35:31.880 --> 35:32.700
It wasn't your

35:32.700 --> 35:33.720
deliberation that was

35:33.720 --> 35:34.340
amortized.

35:34.540 --> 35:35.400
It was the

35:35.400 --> 35:36.340
advertiser's intent.

35:37.060 --> 35:38.080
That is a slightly

35:38.080 --> 35:39.160
terrifying but very

35:39.160 --> 35:40.200
clarifying distinction.

35:40.940 --> 35:42.240
But this brings me to

35:42.240 --> 35:43.620
a massive modern

35:43.620 --> 35:44.460
pushback.

35:44.860 --> 35:45.780
Something that seems to

35:45.780 --> 35:46.580
break all these rules.

35:46.580 --> 35:47.760
What's that?

35:48.200 --> 35:48.980
What about artificial

35:48.980 --> 35:49.580
intelligence?

35:50.240 --> 35:51.100
Specifically, large

35:51.100 --> 35:52.020
language models or

35:52.020 --> 35:53.100
LLMs like the ones we

35:53.100 --> 35:54.000
interact with every day?

35:54.440 --> 35:55.000
Ah, yes.

35:55.600 --> 35:56.540
The AI question.

35:56.920 --> 35:57.860
I can open a chatbot

35:57.860 --> 35:58.360
right now.

35:58.600 --> 35:59.620
Type in a wildly

35:59.620 --> 36:00.580
complex prompt.

36:01.320 --> 36:02.760
Say, write a Shakespearean

36:02.760 --> 36:04.160
sonnet about the

36:04.160 --> 36:05.140
principles of quantum

36:05.140 --> 36:06.260
physics but do it in the

36:06.260 --> 36:07.800
voice of a 17th century

36:07.800 --> 36:08.180
pirate.

36:09.020 --> 36:10.160
And the model outputs

36:10.160 --> 36:11.120
incredibly fluent,

36:11.400 --> 36:12.200
structurally perfect,

36:12.360 --> 36:13.920
complex text in a matter

36:13.920 --> 36:14.500
of milliseconds.

36:14.500 --> 36:15.720
It's uncanny.

36:16.160 --> 36:16.680
It is.

36:17.240 --> 36:18.100
That model never

36:18.100 --> 36:19.500
practiced in a deliberative

36:19.500 --> 36:20.260
conscious way.

36:20.720 --> 36:22.120
It never sat there like

36:22.120 --> 36:23.220
the human novice learning

36:23.220 --> 36:24.720
the piano slowly and

36:24.720 --> 36:25.960
explicitly coordinating

36:25.960 --> 36:27.280
its virtual fingers.

36:27.660 --> 36:28.960
It just spits out

36:28.960 --> 36:29.820
system one level

36:29.820 --> 36:30.800
fluency immediately.

36:31.720 --> 36:32.680
How does aspect

36:32.680 --> 36:33.940
relegation account for a

36:33.940 --> 36:35.020
machine that is

36:35.020 --> 36:36.620
instantly masterful without

36:36.620 --> 36:37.900
ever deliberating?

36:38.260 --> 36:39.020
You've just hit on

36:39.020 --> 36:40.000
perhaps the most

36:40.000 --> 36:40.960
profound and far

36:40.960 --> 36:41.940
reaching concept in the

36:41.940 --> 36:42.760
entire monograph.

36:42.760 --> 36:44.500
inherited compression.

36:45.160 --> 36:46.360
Inherited compression.

36:46.980 --> 36:47.740
Okay, what does that

36:47.740 --> 36:47.940
mean?

36:48.440 --> 36:49.660
Flyxion argues that in

36:49.660 --> 36:50.820
order to achieve a

36:50.820 --> 36:51.820
compressed, fluid,

36:51.980 --> 36:53.100
highly functional output,

36:53.640 --> 36:55.080
exploration must have

36:55.080 --> 36:55.380
occurred.

36:55.760 --> 36:57.360
Someone, somewhere, had to

36:57.360 --> 36:58.100
do the grueling,

36:58.300 --> 36:59.300
effortful work of figuring

36:59.300 --> 37:00.380
out the boundaries of the

37:00.380 --> 37:01.880
problem space, testing what

37:01.880 --> 37:02.980
works and discarding what

37:02.980 --> 37:03.360
doesn't.

37:03.640 --> 37:04.500
The trial and error.

37:04.860 --> 37:05.700
The explicit

37:05.700 --> 37:06.540
deliberation.

37:06.940 --> 37:07.220
Yes.

37:07.740 --> 37:08.880
But, and this is the leap,

37:09.380 --> 37:10.700
that exploration does not

37:10.700 --> 37:11.840
have to be performed by the

37:11.840 --> 37:13.220
agent currently executing

37:13.220 --> 37:13.760
the task.

37:13.960 --> 37:15.180
Oh, wait.

37:15.500 --> 37:16.880
Large language models

37:16.880 --> 37:18.540
possess a vast compression

37:18.540 --> 37:19.380
of statistical

37:19.380 --> 37:21.260
regularities, but those

37:21.260 --> 37:21.980
regularities were

37:21.980 --> 37:23.400
discovered, refined,

37:23.560 --> 37:24.780
and formalized through the

37:24.780 --> 37:26.040
effortful, iterative,

37:26.240 --> 37:28.100
conscious, error-correcting

37:28.100 --> 37:29.080
work of human beings.

37:29.320 --> 37:30.220
All the text they read.

37:30.720 --> 37:32.120
The terabytes of text data

37:32.120 --> 37:33.420
the AI trained on, the

37:33.420 --> 37:34.620
Wikipedia articles, the

37:34.620 --> 37:36.200
books, the forums, the

37:36.200 --> 37:38.120
scientific papers, that

37:38.120 --> 37:39.800
data contains the frozen,

37:39.800 --> 37:41.020
compressed results of

37:41.020 --> 37:42.820
centuries of human explicit

37:42.820 --> 37:43.620
deliberation.

37:44.120 --> 37:44.560
Oh, wow.

37:45.280 --> 37:46.700
So the AI didn't do the

37:46.700 --> 37:48.300
workout, but it inherited

37:48.300 --> 37:48.820
the muscles.

37:49.140 --> 37:49.520
Exactly.

37:50.120 --> 37:51.660
The human race front-loaded

37:51.660 --> 37:52.540
the deliberation.

37:52.760 --> 37:54.000
The AI exhibits fluent,

37:54.180 --> 37:55.540
immediate output without

37:55.540 --> 37:56.640
ever walking the painful

37:56.640 --> 37:57.820
trajectory of explicit

37:57.820 --> 37:58.460
learning itself.

37:58.460 --> 37:59.960
It is utilizing a

37:59.960 --> 38:01.320
transmitted representation.

38:02.200 --> 38:02.880
That makes perfect sense.

38:03.540 --> 38:03.920
Therefore,

38:04.120 --> 38:04.880
Flyxion argues,

38:05.020 --> 38:06.340
it is a profound category

38:06.340 --> 38:07.980
error for AI researchers to

38:07.980 --> 38:09.040
look at a language model's

38:09.040 --> 38:10.720
fast, fluent output, and

38:10.720 --> 38:12.320
declare, ah, this model

38:12.320 --> 38:13.280
has achieved System 1

38:13.280 --> 38:13.820
processing.

38:14.340 --> 38:15.460
Because calling it System

38:15.460 --> 38:16.800
1 implies a specific

38:16.800 --> 38:18.900
biological origin story, a

38:18.900 --> 38:19.800
history of personal

38:19.800 --> 38:21.980
relegation, that the AI just

38:21.980 --> 38:23.020
fundamentally does not

38:23.020 --> 38:23.400
have.

38:23.840 --> 38:25.060
It's wearing the clothes of

38:25.060 --> 38:26.340
mastery without ever having

38:26.340 --> 38:27.180
stepped foot in the gym.

38:27.780 --> 38:28.300
Precisely.

38:28.460 --> 38:29.540
It reproduces the

38:29.540 --> 38:30.660
behavioral signature of

38:30.660 --> 38:32.280
human relegation, but it

38:32.280 --> 38:33.560
does not instantiate the

38:33.560 --> 38:34.760
biological process.

38:35.200 --> 38:36.260
And failing to understand

38:36.260 --> 38:37.440
that distinction is leading

38:37.440 --> 38:38.960
the AI industry down a

38:38.960 --> 38:40.120
very confused path.

38:40.660 --> 38:41.300
Which brings us back to

38:41.300 --> 38:42.500
humans for a moment, and

38:42.500 --> 38:43.580
what I think is the fatal

38:43.580 --> 38:45.120
flaw in the whole two-system

38:45.120 --> 38:45.520
theory.

38:46.060 --> 38:47.180
The thing that, once you

38:47.180 --> 38:48.200
see it, makes the whole

38:48.200 --> 38:49.700
Kahneman framework look a

38:49.700 --> 38:50.140
bit silly.

38:50.380 --> 38:51.920
Oh, the switch problem.

38:52.200 --> 38:52.640
Exactly.

38:53.920 --> 38:55.020
Let's pretend for a moment

38:55.020 --> 38:56.060
that we do believe in

38:56.060 --> 38:57.160
System 1 and System 2.

38:57.720 --> 38:59.040
We have a fast, dumb,

38:59.280 --> 39:00.620
intuitive system, and a

39:00.620 --> 39:01.720
slow, smart, deliberate

39:01.720 --> 39:02.060
system.

39:02.780 --> 39:03.840
If they are separate

39:03.840 --> 39:05.580
systems, how does the

39:05.580 --> 39:06.960
fast system know when to

39:06.960 --> 39:08.100
ask the slow system for

39:08.100 --> 39:08.380
help?

39:08.920 --> 39:10.400
This is a classic paradox

39:10.400 --> 39:11.520
known in the cognitive

39:11.520 --> 39:12.720
literature as the switch

39:12.720 --> 39:13.220
problem.

39:13.780 --> 39:14.900
It is a devastating

39:14.900 --> 39:15.700
critique, heavily

39:15.700 --> 39:16.760
championed by researchers

39:16.760 --> 39:17.780
like Wim Denaeus.

39:18.440 --> 39:19.600
Okay, let me see if I can

39:19.600 --> 39:20.900
explain the paradox of the

39:20.900 --> 39:21.700
switch problem, because

39:21.700 --> 39:22.860
it's a bit of a brain

39:22.860 --> 39:23.120
teaser.

39:23.440 --> 39:23.980
Give it a shot.

39:24.560 --> 39:25.740
If I am driving on

39:25.740 --> 39:27.740
autopilot, System 1 is in

39:27.740 --> 39:28.120
control.

39:28.780 --> 39:29.540
System 1 is, by

39:29.540 --> 39:31.100
definition, fast and

39:31.100 --> 39:31.560
superficial.

39:32.280 --> 39:33.020
It doesn't do deep

39:33.020 --> 39:33.340
reasoning.

39:33.340 --> 39:35.540
Suddenly, a complex,

39:35.720 --> 39:37.040
novel situation arises on

39:37.040 --> 39:37.360
the road.

39:37.620 --> 39:39.080
A multi-car pileup happens

39:39.080 --> 39:39.380
ahead.

39:40.380 --> 39:42.240
For System 2, the smart

39:42.240 --> 39:43.420
reasoning brain, to take

39:43.420 --> 39:45.220
over, System 1 has to

39:45.220 --> 39:46.520
somehow recognize that the

39:46.520 --> 39:48.540
situation is too complex for

39:48.540 --> 39:50.120
its own abilities, and

39:50.120 --> 39:51.260
dispatch a signal to wake

39:51.260 --> 39:52.000
up System 2.

39:52.460 --> 39:53.900
That's the theory.

39:54.200 --> 39:54.620
But wait.

39:55.180 --> 39:56.540
In order to recognize that

39:56.540 --> 39:57.520
a situation is highly

39:57.520 --> 39:59.280
complex and requires deep

39:59.280 --> 40:00.900
reasoning, you have to do

40:00.900 --> 40:01.720
some level of deep

40:01.720 --> 40:03.220
reasoning, which System 1

40:03.220 --> 40:04.400
supposedly cannot do.

40:04.860 --> 40:05.140
Bingo.

40:05.660 --> 40:07.100
So, how can the dumb

40:07.100 --> 40:08.520
system intelligently

40:08.520 --> 40:10.020
dispatch tasks to the

40:10.020 --> 40:10.560
smart system?

40:10.960 --> 40:12.080
You've articulated the

40:12.080 --> 40:12.840
paradox perfectly.

40:13.360 --> 40:14.240
It creates an infinite

40:14.240 --> 40:14.740
regress.

40:15.040 --> 40:15.920
To solve the switch

40:15.920 --> 40:17.020
problem, dual-process

40:17.020 --> 40:18.000
theorists are forced to

40:18.000 --> 40:19.320
either invent a magical,

40:19.600 --> 40:21.060
mysterious third system,

40:21.480 --> 40:22.940
a dispatcher or monitor

40:22.940 --> 40:23.940
that sits above the other

40:23.940 --> 40:25.380
two, which just pushes the

40:25.380 --> 40:26.320
mystery back a step.

40:26.420 --> 40:27.180
Right, a third brain.

40:27.520 --> 40:28.880
Or, they have to admit that

40:28.880 --> 40:30.040
the systems aren't actually

40:30.040 --> 40:30.740
separate at all.

40:31.020 --> 40:31.940
It's like having a security

40:31.940 --> 40:33.120
guard who is asleep at the

40:33.120 --> 40:34.800
desk, but somehow knows

40:34.800 --> 40:36.980
exactly when to wake up to

40:36.980 --> 40:37.800
sound the alarm for a

40:37.800 --> 40:38.200
break-in.

40:38.300 --> 40:38.840
It's impossible.

40:39.380 --> 40:40.640
So, what is Flyxion's

40:40.640 --> 40:41.520
solution to the switch

40:41.520 --> 40:41.840
problem?

40:42.160 --> 40:43.220
Flyxion's solution is

40:43.220 --> 40:43.560
elegant.

40:44.320 --> 40:45.640
There is no switch.

40:46.040 --> 40:46.760
No switch at all.

40:46.840 --> 40:48.120
No switch between systems

40:48.120 --> 40:49.340
because there is only a

40:49.340 --> 40:50.200
single system.

40:50.780 --> 40:51.940
What exists within that

40:51.940 --> 40:53.400
single system is a

40:53.400 --> 40:54.880
continuous embedded

40:54.880 --> 40:56.080
monitoring function.

40:56.360 --> 40:57.260
Okay, we need to break

40:57.260 --> 40:58.820
down how this monitor

40:58.820 --> 41:00.140
physically or conceptually

41:00.140 --> 41:01.980
works because if it's not

41:01.980 --> 41:03.040
a separate dispatcher

41:03.040 --> 41:03.900
system, what is it?

41:04.420 --> 41:05.260
Think of it through the

41:05.260 --> 41:06.080
lens of predictive

41:06.080 --> 41:06.640
processing.

41:07.140 --> 41:08.580
As your relegated routines

41:08.580 --> 41:09.340
run in the background,

41:09.800 --> 41:10.720
they are constantly

41:10.720 --> 41:11.880
generating micro

41:11.880 --> 41:13.200
expectations about what

41:13.200 --> 41:14.360
sensory input should

41:14.360 --> 41:15.000
happen next.

41:15.120 --> 41:15.520
Like what?

41:15.960 --> 41:16.700
When you reach for your

41:16.700 --> 41:17.700
coffee cup without looking,

41:17.920 --> 41:19.200
your brain generates an

41:19.200 --> 41:20.580
expectation of the weight

41:20.580 --> 41:21.760
and temperature of the

41:21.760 --> 41:22.040
ceramic.

41:22.280 --> 41:22.840
Okay, yeah.

41:23.300 --> 41:24.260
The monitor isn't a

41:24.260 --> 41:24.820
separate entity.

41:24.820 --> 41:26.840
It is the inherent friction

41:26.840 --> 41:28.500
of expectation mismatch.

41:28.700 --> 41:29.980
It runs continuously

41:29.980 --> 41:31.460
alongside the relegated

41:31.460 --> 41:33.200
structure, comparing the

41:33.200 --> 41:34.600
incoming sensory data to

41:34.600 --> 41:36.480
the expected sensory data.

41:36.720 --> 41:37.780
So, I reach for the

41:37.780 --> 41:39.300
coffee cup, expecting it to

41:39.300 --> 41:40.840
be full and heavy, but it's

41:40.840 --> 41:41.500
actually empty.

41:41.900 --> 41:43.200
My hand flies up faster than

41:43.200 --> 41:43.740
I intended.

41:44.340 --> 41:45.800
The incoming physical data

41:45.800 --> 41:47.400
mismatches the expectation.

41:47.620 --> 41:48.160
Exactly.

41:48.560 --> 41:49.920
When that mismatch occurs,

41:50.100 --> 41:51.400
when the monitor detects

41:51.400 --> 41:53.200
surprise, error, conflict, or

41:53.200 --> 41:54.960
novelty, it automatically

41:54.960 --> 41:56.960
triggers a widening of the

41:56.960 --> 41:58.260
attentional aperture.

41:58.940 --> 41:59.820
It increases the

41:59.820 --> 42:00.900
resolution of your focus.

42:01.580 --> 42:02.480
The alarm goes off and

42:02.480 --> 42:03.400
the lights turn on in the

42:03.400 --> 42:03.580
room.

42:03.680 --> 42:03.960
Yes.

42:04.480 --> 42:05.740
And this brings us to what

42:05.740 --> 42:07.140
Flyxion considers the

42:07.140 --> 42:08.740
core empirical claim of the

42:08.740 --> 42:10.080
entire monograph, the

42:10.080 --> 42:11.720
concept of selective

42:11.720 --> 42:12.520
scrutiny.

42:13.020 --> 42:14.200
This is how Flyxion

42:14.200 --> 42:15.700
proposes we can actually

42:15.700 --> 42:17.100
prove aspect relegation

42:17.100 --> 42:18.180
theory in a laboratory

42:18.180 --> 42:18.660
setting.

42:19.480 --> 42:20.540
Selective scrutiny.

42:20.860 --> 42:21.040
Yeah.

42:21.820 --> 42:23.020
Contrast this with the old

42:23.020 --> 42:23.340
theory.

42:24.020 --> 42:25.600
If a breakdown triggered a

42:25.600 --> 42:27.120
switch from a fast system

42:27.120 --> 42:29.160
one to a slow system two,

42:29.600 --> 42:31.260
then the entire task would

42:31.260 --> 42:32.160
move to a different mode.

42:32.760 --> 42:34.080
Everything would become slow

42:34.080 --> 42:35.140
and effortful, right?

42:35.660 --> 42:37.620
That is what a global switch

42:37.620 --> 42:38.020
implies.

42:38.160 --> 42:39.240
If you switch engines, the

42:39.240 --> 42:40.380
whole car runs differently.

42:41.020 --> 42:42.360
But Flyxion predicts that

42:42.360 --> 42:43.520
when a relegated routine

42:43.520 --> 42:45.660
breaks down, the return to

42:45.660 --> 42:48.180
explicit conscious control is

42:48.180 --> 42:48.980
highly selective.

42:48.980 --> 42:51.680
It is localized exclusively to

42:51.680 --> 42:53.040
the exact point of failure.

42:53.720 --> 42:54.560
Let's go back to the concert

42:54.560 --> 42:55.920
pianist analogy from the text

42:55.920 --> 42:56.820
because it makes this so

42:56.820 --> 42:57.040
clear.

42:57.680 --> 42:59.160
You have a master pianist

42:59.160 --> 43:00.920
playing a blistering complex

43:00.920 --> 43:01.540
concerto.

43:01.840 --> 43:03.140
They are in a state of flow,

43:03.820 --> 43:05.440
deeply relegated structure.

43:05.640 --> 43:05.880
Right.

43:06.540 --> 43:08.320
Suddenly, halfway through a

43:08.320 --> 43:09.800
measure, their fingering

43:09.800 --> 43:12.260
fails on one specific awkward

43:12.260 --> 43:13.000
chord progression.

43:13.420 --> 43:14.180
They stumble.

43:14.180 --> 43:16.680
If the global switch theory

43:16.680 --> 43:18.920
were true, their entire brain

43:18.920 --> 43:20.980
would slam the brakes, switch

43:20.980 --> 43:22.480
to system two, and they would

43:22.480 --> 43:23.620
suddenly have to consciously

43:23.620 --> 43:24.920
think about everything.

43:25.500 --> 43:26.660
They'd have to consciously

43:26.660 --> 43:27.940
remember how to read the sheet

43:27.940 --> 43:29.420
music, how to sit on the bench,

43:29.500 --> 43:30.740
how to work the foot pedals.

43:30.960 --> 43:31.900
Which would cause them to

43:31.900 --> 43:32.740
completely stop playing.

43:33.420 --> 43:35.140
But in reality, what does an

43:35.140 --> 43:35.560
expert do?

43:35.900 --> 43:37.840
They selectively scrutinize the

43:37.840 --> 43:40.000
fingering of that one specific

43:40.000 --> 43:40.600
passage.

43:40.940 --> 43:41.860
They look at their hand.

43:41.860 --> 43:43.520
They adjust the angle of their

43:43.520 --> 43:44.920
ring finger, and they fix the

43:44.920 --> 43:45.960
localized problem.

43:46.400 --> 43:48.020
They do not reexamine the entire

43:48.020 --> 43:49.680
conceptual foundation of what a

43:49.680 --> 43:50.500
piano is.

43:50.800 --> 43:51.160
Exactly.

43:51.680 --> 43:53.940
The disruption, the slowing down,

43:54.080 --> 43:55.320
and the return of explicit

43:55.320 --> 43:57.360
conscious control are localized

43:57.360 --> 43:58.880
entirely to the affected

43:58.880 --> 43:59.340
component.

44:00.120 --> 44:01.720
The unaffected aspects of playing

44:01.720 --> 44:03.500
the piano, the posture, the

44:03.500 --> 44:04.740
reading ahead, the foot pedals,

44:05.440 --> 44:07.080
remain at their prior deeply

44:07.080 --> 44:08.960
relegated low-resolution state.

44:09.180 --> 44:10.880
To prove this mechanism exists,

44:10.880 --> 44:12.420
Flyxion actually lays out a

44:12.420 --> 44:14.080
proposal for a human study in

44:14.080 --> 44:15.660
Chapter 8, and I want to walk

44:15.660 --> 44:16.820
through the design of this

44:16.820 --> 44:17.620
experiment because it's

44:17.620 --> 44:17.960
brilliant.

44:18.120 --> 44:19.100
It has four phases.

44:19.320 --> 44:19.920
Let's go through it.

44:20.400 --> 44:20.800
Phase 1.

44:21.260 --> 44:22.600
You bring participants into a

44:22.600 --> 44:24.260
lab, and you train them on a

44:24.260 --> 44:25.680
novel task where they have to

44:25.680 --> 44:27.460
explicitly coordinate distinct

44:27.460 --> 44:27.880
components.

44:28.520 --> 44:30.800
For example, a complex motor task

44:30.800 --> 44:32.300
combined with a visual matching

44:32.300 --> 44:32.580
game.

44:32.880 --> 44:34.240
You document their baseline

44:34.240 --> 44:36.200
performance, which will be slow

44:36.200 --> 44:37.060
and effortful.

44:37.560 --> 44:37.880
Right.

44:37.980 --> 44:39.480
They are explicitly tracking all

44:39.480 --> 44:39.900
the pieces.

44:39.900 --> 44:40.840
Phase 2.

44:41.580 --> 44:43.160
You train them extensively until

44:43.160 --> 44:44.780
those components are relegated.

44:44.920 --> 44:45.880
They achieve mastery.

44:46.480 --> 44:47.820
Their speed increases

44:47.820 --> 44:49.500
dramatically, and if you give

44:49.500 --> 44:50.880
them a secondary task to

44:50.880 --> 44:52.420
distract them, their performance

44:52.420 --> 44:53.200
barely drops.

44:53.300 --> 44:54.680
They have reached that state of

44:54.680 --> 44:54.960
flow.

44:55.480 --> 44:56.660
They've compressed the task.

44:57.100 --> 44:57.780
Now Phase 3.

44:58.240 --> 44:59.140
This is the crucial

44:59.140 --> 44:59.720
manipulation.

45:00.520 --> 45:01.920
You perturb one of those

45:01.920 --> 45:03.180
previously coordinated

45:03.180 --> 45:03.720
distinctions.

45:04.020 --> 45:06.440
You quietly change one tiny rule

45:06.440 --> 45:07.860
in the visual matching game, or you

45:07.860 --> 45:09.620
alter the resistance on one of the

45:09.620 --> 45:12.080
motor levers, and then you measure

45:12.080 --> 45:12.820
what happens.

45:12.820 --> 45:14.860
And what we are looking for is the

45:14.860 --> 45:16.040
scope of the disruption.

45:16.540 --> 45:17.840
Does the participant's performance

45:17.840 --> 45:19.700
slowdown globally across the entire

45:19.700 --> 45:21.820
task, or are the errors, the

45:21.820 --> 45:23.640
hesitation, and the participant's

45:23.640 --> 45:25.320
conscious frustration localized

45:25.320 --> 45:27.420
strictly to that one perturbed lever?

45:27.420 --> 45:28.400
Exactly.

45:28.920 --> 45:30.900
And Phase 4 involves a control group.

45:31.100 --> 45:32.180
You have another group of

45:32.180 --> 45:33.680
participants who learn the task

45:33.680 --> 45:35.980
just through raw, unstructured

45:35.980 --> 45:37.620
exposure rather than explicit

45:37.620 --> 45:38.860
step-by-step coordination.

45:39.320 --> 45:41.360
You perturb the same component for

45:41.360 --> 45:42.700
them, and you see if they react

45:42.700 --> 45:43.080
differently.

45:43.380 --> 45:44.740
Because if the control group just

45:44.740 --> 45:47.580
falls apart globally, but the

45:47.580 --> 45:49.040
explicitly trained group can

45:49.040 --> 45:50.420
selectively pinpoint the error...

45:50.420 --> 45:52.740
And it heavily supports aspect

45:52.740 --> 45:53.560
relegation theory.

45:53.960 --> 45:55.520
It proves that the step-by-step

45:55.520 --> 45:57.600
structure was always there in the

45:57.600 --> 45:59.200
trained group's mind, just hidden.

45:59.620 --> 46:01.360
And when the mismatch occurred, the

46:01.360 --> 46:03.200
monitor selectively promoted that

46:03.200 --> 46:05.300
specific hidden structure back to the

46:05.300 --> 46:06.080
surface for repair.

46:07.080 --> 46:09.580
So, if we step back for a second and

46:09.580 --> 46:10.860
look at the big picture of human

46:10.860 --> 46:13.680
mastery through this lens, what does

46:13.680 --> 46:14.580
this all mean for us?

46:15.060 --> 46:18.420
It means that true expertise isn't

46:18.420 --> 46:19.620
about never having to think.

46:20.380 --> 46:21.440
It's not about achieving some

46:21.440 --> 46:23.800
mystical zen state of permanent

46:23.800 --> 46:26.080
system-one autopilot where you just

46:26.080 --> 46:27.400
flow through the universe.

46:27.740 --> 46:28.220
Not at all.

46:28.600 --> 46:31.040
True expertise is about having a

46:31.040 --> 46:33.260
highly-tuned internal alarm system,

46:33.720 --> 46:35.920
a finely calibrated monitor that

46:35.920 --> 46:37.520
knows exactly which tiny,

46:37.760 --> 46:39.680
millimeter-sized part of a routine

46:39.680 --> 46:41.920
needs conscious repair, while

46:41.920 --> 46:43.500
confidently leaving the rest of the

46:43.500 --> 46:44.940
machinery running smoothly in the

46:44.940 --> 46:45.220
dark.

46:45.720 --> 46:47.480
That is the essence of mastery.

46:47.640 --> 46:47.920
It is.

46:47.920 --> 46:50.680
It is a synthesis of well-validated,

46:50.920 --> 46:52.960
relegated structure combined with a

46:52.960 --> 46:55.000
highly sensitive, localized monitor.

46:55.700 --> 46:56.620
I love that definition.

46:56.960 --> 46:58.720
But having this incredibly precise,

46:58.960 --> 47:00.440
functional understanding of human

47:00.440 --> 47:02.580
cognition makes our current attempts

47:02.580 --> 47:04.440
to evaluate artificial intelligence

47:04.440 --> 47:06.260
look almost hilariously sloppy.

47:06.640 --> 47:07.280
It really does.

47:07.620 --> 47:09.560
Which leads us to the philosophy of

47:09.560 --> 47:11.800
science and the very real dangers of

47:11.800 --> 47:13.940
what the text calls model transfer.

47:14.420 --> 47:16.420
Flyxion relies heavily here on the work of

47:16.420 --> 47:18.420
philosopher of science, Mel Andrews.

47:19.060 --> 47:20.820
Andrews writes extensively about the

47:20.820 --> 47:22.620
concept of model transfer and what she

47:22.620 --> 47:24.080
calls hermeneutic shortcuts.

47:24.400 --> 47:25.280
Hermeneutic shortcuts.

47:25.960 --> 47:26.960
I'm not going to lie.

47:27.260 --> 47:28.760
That sounds like a spell from Harry

47:28.760 --> 47:29.040
Potter.

47:29.180 --> 47:30.240
What does it actually mean?

47:30.780 --> 47:32.420
Hermeneutics is the theory and

47:32.420 --> 47:33.720
methodology of interpretation.

47:34.400 --> 47:36.380
A hermeneutic shortcut essentially means

47:36.380 --> 47:38.420
using a pre-existing framework or

47:38.420 --> 47:41.480
vocabulary as an interpretive crutch to

47:41.480 --> 47:43.600
avoid doing the hard foundational work of

47:43.600 --> 47:45.540
understanding what is actually happening in

47:45.540 --> 47:46.180
a new system.

47:46.540 --> 47:46.560
Okay.

47:46.660 --> 47:47.280
That makes sense.

47:47.820 --> 47:49.520
Model transfer occurs when a formal

47:49.520 --> 47:51.600
mathematical model or a set of

47:51.600 --> 47:53.600
vocabulary words developed in one

47:53.600 --> 47:56.020
scientific discipline is enthusiastically

47:56.020 --> 47:58.100
brought over into a completely different

47:58.100 --> 47:58.520
discipline.

47:58.800 --> 48:00.940
But the problem is it brings all of its

48:00.940 --> 48:03.020
original conceptual baggage with it.

48:03.280 --> 48:06.080
The text gives this amazing, almost

48:06.080 --> 48:08.120
comical example to illustrate this, the

48:08.120 --> 48:08.960
plant fallacy.

48:08.960 --> 48:11.340
I want to expand on this because it's so

48:11.340 --> 48:11.900
illuminating.

48:12.320 --> 48:13.380
The Latke-Volterra model.

48:13.760 --> 48:16.020
It's the very famous foundational set of

48:16.020 --> 48:18.480
mathematical equations in ecology and

48:18.480 --> 48:20.720
biology used to describe predator-prey

48:20.720 --> 48:21.720
population dynamics.

48:22.140 --> 48:22.400
Right.

48:22.900 --> 48:25.100
It mathematically models how the population

48:25.100 --> 48:27.540
of foxes and the population of rabbits

48:27.540 --> 48:28.640
oscillate over time.

48:29.280 --> 48:30.780
If there are too many foxes, the rabbits

48:30.780 --> 48:31.360
die off.

48:31.560 --> 48:33.720
Then the foxes starve so their numbers

48:33.720 --> 48:34.140
drop.

48:34.400 --> 48:35.700
Then the rabbits bounce back.

48:35.700 --> 48:38.320
It creates this beautiful, oscillating

48:38.320 --> 48:39.340
mathematical curve.

48:40.280 --> 48:41.900
Now, some researchers in plant biology

48:41.900 --> 48:43.340
were studying a specific plant,

48:43.800 --> 48:44.720
mimosa pudica.

48:45.160 --> 48:47.280
It's a fascinating plant that physically

48:47.280 --> 48:49.580
folds its leaves inward when it is

48:49.580 --> 48:51.740
touched or shaken as a defense mechanism.

48:52.160 --> 48:53.100
I've seen videos of that.

48:53.160 --> 48:53.680
It's really cool.

48:54.260 --> 48:56.440
The researchers discovered that if you

48:56.440 --> 48:58.420
plot the electrical signaling and the

48:58.420 --> 49:00.440
physical leaf folding behavior of this

49:00.440 --> 49:03.280
plant over time, the mathematical curve

49:03.280 --> 49:05.840
matches the Lotka-Volterra equations

49:05.840 --> 49:06.740
perfectly.

49:07.400 --> 49:09.140
Okay, so the math that describes foxes

49:09.140 --> 49:11.780
and rabbits perfectly fits the plant

49:11.780 --> 49:12.740
folding its leaves?

49:12.920 --> 49:14.220
The math fits perfectly.

49:14.640 --> 49:17.080
But here is where the model transfer

49:17.080 --> 49:18.500
goes horribly wrong.

49:19.240 --> 49:21.020
Some researchers in the emerging field

49:21.020 --> 49:23.400
of plant cognition took the perfect fit

49:23.400 --> 49:25.460
of that mathematical model as a

49:25.460 --> 49:27.180
justification to claim that the plant

49:27.180 --> 49:30.280
possesses cognition, learning, and memory.

49:30.520 --> 49:30.960
Oh, wow.

49:30.960 --> 49:32.560
Because the model came from animal

49:32.560 --> 49:34.860
biology, they transferred the model

49:34.860 --> 49:36.820
and they illegally imported the

49:36.820 --> 49:38.920
interpretive baggage of animal brains

49:38.920 --> 49:41.840
into a plant that does not have a

49:41.840 --> 49:42.500
nervous system.

49:42.820 --> 49:44.000
The plant is not a predator.

49:44.360 --> 49:45.100
It is not a prey.

49:45.220 --> 49:45.780
It's a plant.

49:46.500 --> 49:48.300
Just because of the curve of its leaf

49:48.300 --> 49:50.200
folding happens to match a math equation

49:50.200 --> 49:52.280
designed for a fox's doesn't mean the

49:52.280 --> 49:53.380
plant has a secret brain.

49:53.760 --> 49:55.400
It's absurd when you look at it that

49:55.400 --> 49:55.620
way.

49:55.740 --> 49:58.140
It's like, well, if I use a cake recipe's

49:58.140 --> 50:00.620
exact ratios of flour and water to

50:00.620 --> 50:02.260
somehow successfully bake a loaf of

50:02.260 --> 50:04.280
sourdough bread, that doesn't mean the

50:04.280 --> 50:05.380
bread is secretly a cake.

50:05.460 --> 50:07.520
I can't start putting frosting on the

50:07.520 --> 50:08.880
sourdough and telling people it's a

50:08.880 --> 50:09.180
dessert.

50:09.820 --> 50:12.100
We are smuggling in interpretive

50:12.100 --> 50:13.480
baggage based on superficial

50:13.480 --> 50:14.200
similarities.

50:14.860 --> 50:17.300
And Flyxion argues with devastating

50:17.300 --> 50:19.400
clarity that we are doing exactly this

50:19.400 --> 50:22.800
with AI right now, every single day.

50:22.960 --> 50:23.440
Yeah, we are.

50:23.440 --> 50:25.700
When AI engineers and journalists apply

50:25.700 --> 50:27.960
the System 1 and System 2 taxonomy to

50:27.960 --> 50:30.840
large language models, we are using a

50:30.840 --> 50:31.920
hermeneutic shortcut.

50:32.440 --> 50:34.260
We are looking at a neural network, a

50:34.260 --> 50:36.080
massive matrix of mathematical weights.

50:36.660 --> 50:38.680
And because its performance profile looks

50:38.680 --> 50:41.720
fast and fluent, we import the biological

50:41.720 --> 50:44.340
baggage of human cognitive architecture.

50:44.800 --> 50:46.140
We do this constantly in the tech press.

50:46.240 --> 50:48.820
We see a headline that says, new AI achieves

50:48.820 --> 50:50.500
doctoral level performance in physics.

50:50.500 --> 50:53.600
And we assign all this human weight to

50:53.600 --> 50:54.180
that phrase.

50:54.680 --> 50:54.960
Yes.

50:55.140 --> 50:57.760
When we use the phrase doctoral level, we

50:57.760 --> 51:00.400
are illegally importing the baggage of

51:00.400 --> 51:02.160
what a human PhD entails.

51:02.520 --> 51:04.380
Think about what a human with a doctorate

51:04.380 --> 51:05.160
actually does.

51:05.340 --> 51:07.040
They don't just answer multiple choice

51:07.040 --> 51:08.360
trivia questions very quickly.

51:08.580 --> 51:09.260
Obviously not.

51:09.640 --> 51:12.220
A human PhD formulates completely original

51:12.220 --> 51:13.160
research questions.

51:13.520 --> 51:15.360
They navigate lab politics.

51:15.600 --> 51:18.180
They recognize when a new anomalous piece

51:18.180 --> 51:20.000
of evidence completely undermines their

51:20.000 --> 51:20.880
multi-year project.

51:20.880 --> 51:23.540
And they suffer the emotional toll of

51:23.540 --> 51:24.600
revising their worldview.

51:25.360 --> 51:27.660
A benchmark test score, which is all the

51:27.660 --> 51:30.140
AI achieved, measures absolutely none of

51:30.140 --> 51:30.340
that.

51:31.040 --> 51:32.880
We are projecting the human journey, the

51:32.880 --> 51:35.440
struggle, the relegation, the monitor, onto

51:35.440 --> 51:37.040
the machine's static output.

51:38.180 --> 51:40.060
Flyxion even argues that importing the

51:40.060 --> 51:43.280
word intelligence into artificial intelligence

51:43.280 --> 51:44.320
does this.

51:44.320 --> 51:48.600
The word implies a generalized adaptive capacity that

51:48.600 --> 51:51.720
isn't actually being measured by predicting the next

51:51.720 --> 51:52.740
token in a sentence.

51:53.860 --> 51:56.600
And armed with this skepticism of borrowed language, we

51:56.600 --> 52:00.120
can finally turn a critical eye toward the biggest, most

52:00.120 --> 52:02.400
hyped trend in the AI industry right now.

52:02.680 --> 52:03.880
Oh, this is the hot topic.

52:04.260 --> 52:05.520
Inference time compute.

52:06.260 --> 52:07.720
Giving models more time to think.

52:08.360 --> 52:08.920
Right.

52:08.920 --> 52:12.780
If you follow AI at all, you know that the current

52:12.780 --> 52:16.140
obsession is allowing LLMs to generate long, hidden,

52:16.800 --> 52:18.960
intermediate outputs before they finally give you an

52:18.960 --> 52:19.240
answer.

52:19.980 --> 52:23.120
Techniques like chain of thought reasoning, having the

52:23.120 --> 52:26.580
model sample multiple candidate answers, letting the model

52:26.580 --> 52:28.520
check its own work in a hidden scratch pad.

52:28.520 --> 52:32.980
And the entire tech industry, from the CEOs to the marketing

52:32.980 --> 52:36.160
departments, is universally calling this process giving the

52:36.160 --> 52:37.160
AI system two.

52:37.640 --> 52:38.020
It's everywhere.

52:38.660 --> 52:42.020
They say the base model responding instantly is system one.

52:42.700 --> 52:45.620
But if we give it this scratch pad and force it to think out

52:45.620 --> 52:49.200
loud before it answers, we have unlocked system two reasoning.

52:49.560 --> 52:54.020
But Flyxion uses the framework of aspect relegation to completely

52:54.020 --> 52:54.980
dismantle this idea.

52:55.380 --> 52:56.500
Let's break this down.

52:56.500 --> 52:59.360
How does the theory counter this tech industry narrative?

53:00.220 --> 53:02.400
Well, first, we have to ground ourselves in the physical,

53:02.980 --> 53:04.920
mathematical reality of the model itself.

53:05.520 --> 53:09.380
When a language model is answering a prompt, what developers call

53:09.380 --> 53:12.960
inference time, its neural weights are entirely fixed.

53:13.440 --> 53:14.680
The training process is over.

53:15.040 --> 53:15.880
The brain is baked.

53:16.440 --> 53:17.260
The cement is dry.

53:17.260 --> 53:20.980
The structural topology of the network is set in stone.

53:21.420 --> 53:26.260
Therefore, giving the model more time to output text or giving it a

53:26.260 --> 53:30.160
hidden scratch pad, does not magically spawn a new cognitive faculty.

53:30.660 --> 53:34.440
It does not build a new system two engine inside the code.

53:35.180 --> 53:36.200
So what does it do?

53:36.940 --> 53:40.820
All it does is increase the computational budget for the existing structure to

53:40.820 --> 53:41.380
operate.

53:41.660 --> 53:45.720
It allows the model's existing fixed weights to be exercised at a higher

53:45.720 --> 53:50.680
volume, feeding intermediate textual results back into the exact same fixed

53:50.680 --> 53:51.280
network.

53:51.280 --> 53:53.500
But let me make sure I'm wrapping my head around this.

53:54.220 --> 53:57.140
It's like giving me more time to take a standardized math test.

53:57.560 --> 54:03.200
If I simply do not know calculus, if the structure isn't in my brain, giving me three

54:03.200 --> 54:07.800
extra hours to stare at the test isn't going to magically spawn a calculus module in my

54:07.800 --> 54:08.080
head.

54:08.300 --> 54:08.680
Exactly.

54:09.080 --> 54:11.020
I'm not going to invent calculus on the spot.

54:11.140 --> 54:16.380
I'm just going to apply my existing basic algebra skills more thoroughly over and over,

54:16.380 --> 54:20.540
or maybe draw some really detailed high resolution doodles in the margins.

54:21.120 --> 54:25.180
The output volume increases, but the fundamental capability hasn't changed.

54:25.440 --> 54:26.440
That is exactly right.

54:26.740 --> 54:28.540
More churn does not equal a new system.

54:29.080 --> 54:35.020
And Flyxion details a specific AI architecture from recent research to prove how a network can

54:35.020 --> 54:39.400
actually learn a procedure rather than just memorizing answers without needing a magical

54:39.400 --> 54:40.280
second system.

54:40.500 --> 54:44.120
It's called the PAR model, progress aligned recurrence.

54:44.120 --> 54:47.600
Okay, let's get slightly technical, but keep it accessible.

54:48.380 --> 54:49.900
How does the PAR model work?

54:50.640 --> 54:54.660
A standard LLM pushes data through its layers once and spits out a word.

54:55.360 --> 55:01.340
The PAR model takes a block of those layers and loops them, repeating the computation a variable

55:01.340 --> 55:03.720
number of times before outputting the final answer.

55:04.060 --> 55:04.820
Okay, looping.

55:05.520 --> 55:08.880
They train this model on sequential state tracking tasks.

55:08.880 --> 55:13.880
Think of a digital shell game where the model has to keep track of a hidden object as cups are

55:13.880 --> 55:15.380
moved around over multiple steps.

55:15.680 --> 55:21.080
But crucially, during training, they force the model to predict the intermediate states.

55:21.620 --> 55:23.660
What is an intermediate state in this context?

55:24.140 --> 55:25.300
Let's use an analogy.

55:25.860 --> 55:27.660
Think of it like a chef's mixing bowl.

55:27.980 --> 55:33.520
If the task is to bake a cake, a standard LLM just tries to predict the final image of the

55:33.520 --> 55:34.080
baked cake.

55:34.080 --> 55:39.860
The PAR model is forced to predict what the mixing bowl looks like after the flour is added,

55:40.020 --> 55:43.840
then what it looks like after the eggs are added, then what it looks like after it's stirred.

55:44.140 --> 55:46.740
Those are the latent intermediate states.

55:47.280 --> 55:50.920
So by forcing it to predict the mixing bowl at every step, it is actually learning the

55:50.920 --> 55:54.460
procedure of baking, not just memorizing the final picture of the cake.

55:54.760 --> 55:55.240
Exactly.

55:55.780 --> 56:01.860
Practice here teaches an actual reusable structural procedure through looping these latent states.

56:01.860 --> 56:07.400
And what is fascinating about the PAR model is that it relies heavily on a learned halting

56:07.400 --> 56:07.860
signal.

56:08.180 --> 56:08.740
A halting signal?

56:09.460 --> 56:11.740
The model has to learn when to stop looping its layers.

56:11.880 --> 56:15.780
It has to learn when the answer in the mixing bowl is good enough to put in the oven.

56:16.020 --> 56:18.200
If it stops too early, the answer is wrong.

56:18.500 --> 56:24.340
But interestingly, if it keeps computing over thinking past the correct answer, the performance

56:24.340 --> 56:25.160
actually degrades.

56:25.440 --> 56:30.220
So knowing when to stop thinking is just as mathematically important as the thinking itself.

56:30.220 --> 56:34.140
Which perfectly mirrors the human monitoring problem we discussed earlier.

56:34.740 --> 56:39.540
You need a monitor to tell you when to widen your attention and when to narrow it back down

56:39.540 --> 56:40.460
and just act.

56:41.340 --> 56:45.160
But the critical takeaway for evaluating modern AI is this.

56:45.800 --> 56:50.760
How do we test if an AI chatbot actually has this monitoring capability?

56:51.520 --> 56:56.880
Flyxion proposes a behavioral test for AI, directly mirroring the selective scrutiny test

56:56.880 --> 56:57.880
proposed for humans.

56:57.880 --> 57:00.700
The controlled mismatch experiment for AI.

57:01.220 --> 57:01.800
How does it work?

57:02.240 --> 57:06.660
You give the AI a very familiar structurally rigid reasoning task.

57:06.780 --> 57:12.160
Say a complex logic puzzle that it has seen millions of variations of in its training data.

57:12.600 --> 57:15.900
It has a deeply relegated default routine for solving it.

57:16.060 --> 57:16.700
Easy for it.

57:16.860 --> 57:19.080
But you introduce a controlled mismatch.

57:19.440 --> 57:22.680
You subtly alter one specific premise in step three of the puzzle.

57:22.680 --> 57:26.340
So that the default routine will yield a wrong answer.

57:27.020 --> 57:29.700
Then you give the AI a massive inference budget.

57:30.020 --> 57:31.660
You tell it to use chain of thought.

57:31.980 --> 57:32.720
Take its time.

57:33.000 --> 57:34.100
Write a huge scratch pad.

57:34.620 --> 57:35.880
And what are we looking for in the output?

57:36.380 --> 57:39.360
We want to see if the model has true selective scrutiny.

57:40.020 --> 57:42.440
Does the model recognize that step three is anomalous?

57:42.800 --> 57:43.920
Halt its default routine?

57:43.920 --> 57:49.300
And allocate all of that extra computation specifically to repairing the logic of step three?

57:49.860 --> 57:50.440
And if it doesn't?

57:51.080 --> 57:56.940
Well, does it just blindly increase global scrutiny, turning out pages and pages of irrelevant text

57:56.940 --> 58:01.660
across all the steps without ever realizing where the actual structural breakdown occurred?

58:01.660 --> 58:06.480
If it just uniformly turns out text everywhere, it means it doesn't have a monitor.

58:06.660 --> 58:08.920
It doesn't have true selective scrutiny.

58:09.500 --> 58:12.900
It's just running the exact same fixed weights, but longer.

58:13.540 --> 58:19.980
And if it fails that test, it leads to Flyxion's ultimate defining conclusion about the state of artificial intelligence today.

58:20.620 --> 58:22.160
The relocation of the deficit.

58:22.660 --> 58:23.820
Relocating the deficit.

58:24.080 --> 58:24.380
Yes.

58:25.080 --> 58:30.020
The AI industry is entirely wrong to say these models lack system two reasoning.

58:30.020 --> 58:31.960
Slowness is not magic.

58:32.600 --> 58:37.200
Generating long, slow chains of thought in a hidden text box does not automatically make

58:37.200 --> 58:39.820
an AI rational or capable of deep reasoning.

58:40.880 --> 58:44.760
So, if they don't lack system two, what do they actually lack?

58:45.140 --> 58:45.820
Let's bring it home.

58:46.280 --> 58:51.000
What modern AI actually lacks is endogenous control of resolution.

58:51.660 --> 58:52.700
Endogenous control.

58:53.340 --> 58:54.960
Meaning generated from within.

58:55.140 --> 58:55.720
Self-directed.

58:55.860 --> 58:56.180
Yes.

58:56.180 --> 59:03.360
The self-directed internal ability to adaptively re-promote hidden structure when a default compressed routine

59:03.360 --> 59:03.920
breaks down.

59:04.760 --> 59:06.280
Humans can feel when a habit is failing.

59:06.740 --> 59:08.040
Our internal monitor spikes.

59:08.400 --> 59:10.200
We pinpoint the exact point of failure.

59:10.460 --> 59:15.620
And we selectively widen our attentional aperture to fix that specific millimeter of the problem.

59:15.900 --> 59:16.680
We self-correct.

59:17.120 --> 59:20.240
Current AI models largely lack that internal monitor.

59:20.240 --> 59:25.580
They lack the capacity to detect when their default statistical compression is inappropriate

59:25.580 --> 59:26.820
for a novel environment.

59:27.080 --> 59:30.760
And they lack the ability to selectively raise their internal resolution to fix it.

59:31.080 --> 59:32.440
That is the true deficit.

59:32.740 --> 59:34.820
Not a missing magical system, too.

59:35.880 --> 59:36.100
Okay.

59:36.180 --> 59:41.540
If you are listening to this, I hope your mind is as thoroughly blown as mine was reading this.

59:41.540 --> 59:47.220
Because if we synthesize everything we have covered today, we have completely demolished the dual

59:47.220 --> 59:47.940
process theory.

59:48.620 --> 59:54.240
The idea of a fast emotional system one and a slow rational system two is a myth.

59:54.840 --> 59:59.320
It is a fairy tale born from bad analogies and laboratory operational drift.

59:59.320 --> 01:00:06.440
We have replaced that myth with a much more powerful framework, aspect relegation, the understanding

01:00:06.440 --> 01:00:13.620
that human practice compresses explicit high-resolution coordination into untracked but still actively

01:00:13.620 --> 01:00:15.020
running internal structure.

01:00:15.500 --> 01:00:17.020
We've learned that difficulty isn't real.

01:00:17.460 --> 01:00:19.980
Well, it's real, but it's not a property of the universe.

01:00:20.720 --> 01:00:25.260
Difficulty is just a relationship between a task and your personal history governed by the

01:00:25.260 --> 01:00:27.340
amortized cost of your past deliberations.

01:00:27.340 --> 01:00:31.980
And we have completely reframed how to look at the artificial intelligence systems that

01:00:31.980 --> 01:00:33.820
are supposedly about to run our world.

01:00:34.300 --> 01:00:39.940
We have stripped away the hermeneutic baggage of reasoning and systems and focused on what

01:00:39.940 --> 01:00:40.780
actually matters.

01:00:41.280 --> 01:00:46.520
Inherited compression, fixed weights, and the vital necessity of regulating resolution.

01:00:46.980 --> 01:00:50.960
The tech world is desperately trying to build AI a slow, rational brain.

01:00:51.600 --> 01:00:53.000
But slowness isn't magic.

01:00:53.460 --> 01:00:56.020
Churning out more text doesn't make a machine smarter.

01:00:56.020 --> 01:00:59.980
What AI lacks is a self-awareness alarm.

01:01:00.440 --> 01:01:03.880
It doesn't know when it's messing up, so it doesn't know when to pay closer attention.

01:01:04.380 --> 01:01:06.320
It is a massive paradigm shift.

01:01:06.820 --> 01:01:11.920
It takes the mystery out of human intuition, and it takes the magic out of AI's slowness.

01:01:12.480 --> 01:01:13.660
It really does.

01:01:13.880 --> 01:01:17.240
But I want to leave you, the listener, with a final provocative thought.

01:01:17.740 --> 01:01:21.760
Something that builds on everything we've discussed today, but applies directly to your

01:01:21.760 --> 01:01:22.740
life right now.

01:01:24.020 --> 01:01:27.420
Consider the monitoring cost in your own daily routines.

01:01:27.420 --> 01:01:33.360
It is the most vital and most often neglected parameter in Flyxion's equation.

01:01:34.100 --> 01:01:35.040
Think about it.

01:01:35.460 --> 01:01:41.480
If our intuition, our gut feeling, is just deeply relegated structure, as Flyxion argues,

01:01:41.980 --> 01:01:46.920
it means our intuition is incredibly vulnerable to silent failures when the environment changes.

01:01:47.680 --> 01:01:51.660
Our deeply ingrained habits carry an implicit, hidden assumption.

01:01:51.660 --> 01:01:56.520
They assume that the world today is exactly the same as the world was on the day we first

01:01:56.520 --> 01:01:57.220
learned the habit.

01:01:57.580 --> 01:01:59.600
Which is rarely the case forever.

01:01:59.840 --> 01:02:00.140
Right.

01:02:00.340 --> 01:02:06.320
So ask yourself, what deeply amortized habit or intuitive judgment are you relying on today

01:02:06.320 --> 01:02:09.640
in an environment that has fundamentally changed underneath you?

01:02:10.220 --> 01:02:15.080
What untracked background distinctions in your career, in your relationships, or in your

01:02:15.080 --> 01:02:21.220
worldviews desperately need to be promoted back to full conscious resolution before they silently

01:02:21.220 --> 01:02:21.580
fail?

01:02:21.980 --> 01:02:28.000
It is ultimately a question of where and when you are selectively allocating your attention.

01:02:28.300 --> 01:02:28.760
Exactly.

01:02:29.240 --> 01:02:31.540
Your cognitive x-ray machine isn't broken.

01:02:32.300 --> 01:02:34.580
You just need to know exactly where to point it.

01:02:35.140 --> 01:02:36.940
Thank you for taking this plunge with us today.

01:02:37.680 --> 01:02:41.860
Keep questioning the structures you've relegated and keep your monitor active.

01:02:41.860 --> 01:02:42.880
Take care.

